Play in Group B of the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]] began on 10 June and completed on 20 June 2006. [[England national football team|England]] won the group, and advanced to the round of 16, along with [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]]. [[Paraguay national football team|Paraguay]] and [[Trinidad and Tobago national football team|Trinidad and Tobago]] were eliminated.<ref>{{cite web |last=Saaid |first=Hamdan |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2006full.html |title=World Cup 2006 – Match Details |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=7 February 2007 |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

==Background==
Group B was the second of eight groups to start play at the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]] in Germany. The competition consisted of 32 competitors, split into eight groups of four teams. The sides would play each other on a [[Round-robin tournament|round-robin basis]] with the top two teams in each group advancing to the round of 16.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/newsfiles/19085.pdf |title=Regulations 2006 FIFA World Cup Germany|format=PDF | publisher=FIFA |accessdate=11 January 2023}}</ref>

